  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "cancer-spatial-c91c",
  "summary": "Integrating single-cell, spatial and bulk data is nominating prognostic states, but most findings remain exploratory and computationally derived.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is integrative profiling of tumour microenvironment composition, pairing single-cell or spatial transcriptomics with bulk cohorts to nominate prognostic genes, cell states and pathways. Examples in this set include an ACKR1+ endothelial lactate-immune signature associated with carotid plaque vulnerability, an epi8 epithelial subcluster that stratifies cervical carcinoma risk, and THBS1+ macrophages with a putative THBS1-CD36 axis in coronary atherosclerosis. Newer elements include exploratory MOFA+ integration of paired scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq from two NMIBC patients, which identifies a BCG-associated HSPC latent factor with an adverse prognostic association in tumour, and radiogenomic links between a CT-defined high-risk phenotype and transcription factor regulatory states in NSCLC. Several findings remain exploratory, and the set also includes a review of circulating proteomic multicancer early detection studies.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-07"
}
